LICENSE-UPSTREAM-MIT and NOTICE-UPSTREAM.

Protocol comparison reference:
https://github.com/FDH2/UxPlay/tree/48f5ce47c9ef694afccfac907c9e8828329657fe

Changes in this native ESP-IDF port:
- Public callback API and persistent NVS receiver identity.
- Finite startup/shutdown, bounded RTSP and mirror packet handling.
- Checked binary-plist arithmetic, AVCC validation, multi-SPS/PPS extraction.
- Session peer binding, explicit failure codes and no-video diagnostics.
- Timing sockets start at the first SETUP, as in UxPlay.
- Completed legacy-pairing requirement before hashing the session AES key.
- Relative sender timestamps and SPS/PPS-prefixed IDR callbacks.
- Const-correct PlayFair table access; cryptographic algorithms are retained.
- No Arduino, GStreamer, iPhone relay app, or HoppScreen sender dependency.

No macOS/physical-board end-to-end compatibility or performance is claimed.
This component does not implement Sidecar, Apple Pencil, Touch Bar, or iPad identity.

The linked firmware is a combined GPL work; distribute its corresponding source
and the applicable dependency notices with binaries. libsodium and mDNS retain
their own upstream licenses in the managed-component packages.
